@@ -18,6 +18,17 @@ exponent drives an anti-aliased superellipse in the D3D11 pixel shader. The WPF
 fallback uses the closest circular Win32 region because `CreateRoundRectRgn`
 cannot represent a continuous superellipse.
 
+## Preview aspect
+
+Each profile also carries its device family's native portrait panel
+resolution. `DeviceCornerProfileResolver.ResolveScreenSize` returns the
+device-reported stream geometry when a frame already exists, and otherwise the
+ProductType family's panel, so a preview window starts at the real device
+screen ratio instead of one hard-coded phone shape. Senders with no device
+screen (Apple TV, video-app casting) report no size and keep the historical
+default. The D3D11 renderer always letterboxes to the decoded frame aspect, so
+the picture is never cropped or stretched whatever the window ratio is.
+
